{% set local_problem %}
<p>Tanner's housing mix creates varied gutter challenges. Newer subdivisions often have builder-grade sectional gutters that meet minimum code but can't handle real storms. When heavy rainfall hits, these undersized systems overflow and send water toward foundations instead of away.</p>

<p>Established Tanner homes face different problems. Original gutters have weathered decades of North Alabama weather. Seams have failed, hangers have loosened, and the cumulative effects of humidity and temperature swings have taken their toll. Many of these homes still have sectional gutters with failing seams at every 10-foot joint.</p>

<p>The area's clay soil makes gutter problems worse. Unlike sandy soil that absorbs water, clay forces runoff to pool and spread. When gutters overflow, that water doesn't disappear — it accumulates around your foundation.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate the seam problem entirely. Custom-fabricated on-site to fit your home exactly, they have no weak points to fail. For Tanner homes, seamless gutters provide the reliable protection our weather demands.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Tanner home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline.</p>
{% endset %}

